<section class="wm-hero" style="margin-top:68px">
  <div class="eyebrow">Work With Me</div>
  <h1>Senior design leadership, <em>and the hands</em> to back it up</h1>
  <p>I partner with companies that need senior design leadership and the hands to back it up. Sometimes that's a full-time executive role. Sometimes it's a fractional engagement where you get the strategy, the team-building, and the craft without the full-time hire. Either way I sit on the same side of the table as you and your team, focused on what we can actually ship.</p>
</section>
<div class="wm-heroimg"><img src="assets/work/work-with-me-hero.jpg" alt="Aneil Razvi facilitating a workshop, with the logos of companies he has run sessions for" width="2000" height="1250"></div>

<div class="wm-tabs">
  <div class="wm-tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Two ways to work together">
    <button class="wm-tab" id="tab-work" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-work" type="button">Work with me</button>
    <button class="wm-tab" id="tab-workshop" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-workshop" tabindex="-1" type="button">Workshop with me</button>
  </div>
  <p class="wm-tabnote" id="tabnote">An engagement is a season. A workshop is a day. Most people start with the second one.</p>
</div>


<div id="panel-work" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-work">
<section class="wm-sec">
  <h2>What I can do for you</h2>
  <div class="wm-services">
    <div class="wm-card"><h3>Fractional Head or VP of Design, or CXO</h3><p>Set the design direction, build and coach the team, and raise the bar on craft and process.</p></div>
    <div class="wm-card"><h3>AI experience strategy</h3><p>Define where AI genuinely belongs in your product, and a framework your team can design against, instead of bolting on features.</p></div>
    <div class="wm-card"><h3>0-to-1 and R&D</h3><p>Take a concept from someone's head to a working, shippable product with a lean team and a fast clock.</p></div>
    <div class="wm-card"><h3>Design org and operations</h3><p>Stand up the function, set the career ladders and rituals, and build the research and design-ops backbone that lets it scale.</p></div>
    <div class="wm-card"><h3>Brand and experience direction</h3><p>Identity, motion, and the through-line that makes a product feel like one thing.</p></div>
    <div class="wm-card"><h3>Design maturity assessment</h3><p>Figure out whether you're ready for design and research, and at what level: AI-assisted, fractional, contract, agency, or a full team. A clear read, not a pitch for a big hire.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wm-maturity">
  <div class="wm-maturity-in">
    <div class="eyebrow">Start here if you're not sure</div>
    <h2>How much design do you actually need?</h2>
    <p class="sub">Most companies over-invest in design too early or starve it for too long. Before you hire anyone, I'll read where your org actually is and point you to the right level of investment for your stage.</p>
    <div class="wm-ladder">
      <div class="rung"><div class="lvl">Level 01</div><h4>AI-assisted</h4><p>The right tools, no dedicated designers. Enough to ship and learn while design isn't the bottleneck yet.</p></div>
      <div class="rung"><div class="lvl">Level 02</div><h4>Fractional lead</h4><p>One senior designer, part-time. Direction and craft without a full-time hire. Often where I come in.</p></div>
      <div class="rung"><div class="lvl">Level 03</div><h4>Independent contractors</h4><p>A few specialists for the moment. Flexible hands when the work comes in bursts.</p></div>
      <div class="rung"><div class="lvl">Level 04</div><h4>External firm</h4><p>An agency for a big, bounded push. Capacity and polish, on a clock.</p></div>
      <div class="rung"><div class="lvl">Level 05</div><h4>In-house team</h4><p>A built-out design org. The right call once design is core to how you compete.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="closer">I'll tell you which rung you're actually on, even when the honest answer is "you don't need me yet." I would rather lose the work than sell you the wrong shape of it.</p>
    <p style="margin:1.8rem 0 0"><a href="maturity.html" style="display:inline-block;background:#00BCD4;color:#0F1923;font-weight:700;font-size:.98rem;padding:.85rem 1.8rem;border-radius:99px;text-decoration:none">Take the assessment, free</a>
    <span style="display:block;color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);font-size:.85rem;margin-top:.7rem">About four minutes. The full read comes by email.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wm-sec" style="background:#0c1620;max-width:none;padding-left:0;padding-right:0">
  <div style="max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 6%">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <div class="wm-steps">
      <div class="wm-step"><span class="n">01</span><h3>Talk</h3><p>A short conversation about where you are and what is in the way.</p></div>
      <div class="wm-step"><span class="n">02</span><h3>Scope</h3><p>We pick the shape together: usually a one to two days a week retainer, sometimes a scoped sprint. You start in days, not months.</p></div>
      <div class="wm-step"><span class="n">03</span><h3>Ship</h3><p>Embedded with your team from week one. Senior judgment and hands-on work, not a deck and a goodbye.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wm-sec">
  <h2>Recommendations</h2>
  <div class="wm-recs">
